WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.133
This is a closer look at the Copilot
Credit Estimator — the four

2
00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:09.667
ways to build an estimate, and how a
single estimate carries all

3
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:14.200
the way through to return on investment
and a finished proposal.

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.298
It always begins by choosing how you want
to estimate.

5
00:00:18.298 --> 00:00:21.409
There are four ways in, and the right one

6
00:00:21.409 --> 00:00:24.900
depends on how far along your idea already
is.

7
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.178
Quick takes a plain-English description.

8
00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:33.176
Quick plus Import sizes a whole portfolio
from a spreadsheet.

9
00:00:33.176 --> 00:00:38.339
Detailed lets you set your org scope and
dial in every feature.

10
00:00:38.339 --> 00:00:42.600
And Solution package reads a built agent
you upload.

11
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.209
Let's follow the most common path — Quick.

12
00:00:46.209 --> 00:00:50.162
You describe the agent in ordinary words:
what

13
00:00:50.162 --> 00:00:54.544
it does, who uses it, how often, and where
it runs.

14
00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:59.700
An example chip fills in a realistic
scenario to start from.

15
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.651
Selecting Build my estimate reads your

16
00:01:02.651 --> 00:01:06.767
description and pre-fills a short, guided
assessment.

17
00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:10.417
Confirm a few quick questions, or skip
straight

18
00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:14.300
to results — your live estimate updates as
you go.

19
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.696
The result is three plain numbers: the
build

20
00:01:17.696 --> 00:01:21.401
size, the monthly credits, and the monthly
cost.

21
00:01:21.401 --> 00:01:25.723
It even outlines how the agent would be
built in Copilot

22
00:01:25.723 --> 00:01:30.200
Studio, and lets you flip the engine to
compare licensing.

23
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.742
When you already know the building blocks,
switch to Detailed.

24
00:01:34.742 --> 00:01:38.625
Here you set the total users in scope, how
often they

25
00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:43.900
interact, and then dial in exactly which
features each interaction uses.

26
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:48.421
Every row — a classic answer, a generative
answer, an

27
00:01:48.421 --> 00:01:53.625
agent action, tenant grounding — carries
its own credit rate.

28
00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:59.000
As you fill them in, the monthly total
builds up, line by line.

29
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.496
If the agent is already built, Solution
package is the most precise.

30
00:02:04.496 --> 00:02:09.184
Export it from Power Platform as a dot-zip
and drop it in.

31
00:02:09.184 --> 00:02:12.901
It's parsed entirely in your browser —
nothing

32
00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:16.700
is uploaded — and sized component by
component.

33
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.601
And when you're sizing many agents at
once, Quick

34
00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:24.342
plus Import takes a simple Excel template
— one

35
00:02:24.342 --> 00:02:28.800
row per scenario — and returns a
portfolio-wide roll-up.

36
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.625
Whichever mode you use, you land on the
same estimate,

37
00:02:32.625 --> 00:02:36.308
and the same two ways forward: refine the
numbers in

38
00:02:36.308 --> 00:02:40.700
Detailed, or turn them into a business
case with Estimate ROI.

39
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.005
The ROI Estimator adds your economics —

40
00:02:44.005 --> 00:02:48.072
minutes saved per task and a loaded hourly
rate.

41
00:02:48.072 --> 00:02:52.139
It returns a payback period, a return over
three

42
00:02:52.139 --> 00:02:56.800
years, and a net value, bracketed by a
confidence band.

43
00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:02.187
One more step — Add to proposal —
assembles everything into a clean,

44
00:03:02.187 --> 00:03:07.258
one-page business case: the problem, your
approach, the solution

45
00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:13.200
sizing, and the value and ROI, ready to
copy or print for a funding review.

46
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.713
That's the full journey — from a
plain-English idea, to a

47
00:03:18.713 --> 00:03:25.000
credit estimate, to ROI, to a proposal a
budget owner can act on.

